# @file Silence Suzuka - Recruitment
# @author 牛蛙煲
# @author Katze (translator)
start:
  title: First Encounter
  lines:
    - Early dawn, in the Trainer's office.
    - Despite having zero desire to sleep, %YOU% still fought back a yawn.
    - Right now, sitting on the left side of %YOU%'s desk was a peculiar aluminum can, faintly sporting a smiling dark-haired %UMA% on its label.
    - And on the right lay a small mountain of already processed paperwork.
    - 「If only I hadn't succumbed to curiosity and tried that "Special %UMA% Brew Coffee"... Now I probably won't even be able to sleep tomorrow night...」
    - %YOU% let out a helpless, weary sigh and pushed back from the desk.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Might as well take a walk outside. I'm wide awake anyway...」
    - In the end, %YOU% threw on a warm jacket, quietly pulled the office door shut, and stepped out into the chill.
    - Dawn over Tracen Academy.
    - Although the academy housed countless %UMA%, their trainers, and faculty members, it was far too early for almost anyone to be out and about.
    - The campus was cloaked in a tranquil, peaceful silence; everyone was undoubtedly fast asleep in bed.
    - Everyone except %YOU%.
    - With hands shoved deep into pockets, %YOU% wandered aimlessly through the expansive grounds, still buzzing from that cursed can of coffee.
    - Walking down Tracen's main avenue and gazing at the distant buildings, %YOU%'s mind began to wander.
    - 「If one day I actually make it big and become a legendary trainer written into the history books...」
    - acc: 1
      content: 「I'll be sure to endorse that brain-jolting %UMA% coffee to everyone.」
    - Chuckling quietly, %YOU% was amused by the absurd thought.
    - Because of that distraction, %YOU% failed to notice the light, rhythmic footsteps approaching from behind.
    - That is, until a slender, delicate hand gently tapped the grinning %YOU% right on the shoulder.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: '???'
        - 「Um... excuse me? Mister Ghost, or mister mystery man... hello?」
    - Like a classic protagonist in a horror flick, %YOU% went pale in an instant, expression freezing solid, and turned around frame by frame toward the voice.
    - The first thing that caught %YOU%'s eye was a pair of cute, distinctive green ear covers. Below them fell sleek, silky lengths of orange hair.
    - She wore Tracen Academy's red training jersey, clearly a student here.
    - %SEX% seemed to have run quite a distance; faint breaths rose in gentle white puffs from her lips.
    - Just then, the unfamiliar Young %UMA% noticed the Trainer badge pinned to %YOU%'s chest, immediately grasping %YOU%'s identity.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Young %UMA%
        - 「Oh, you're an Academy Trainer! I'm not sure why you're up so early, but I have to get back to my morning run. See you around, Trainer!」
    - The Young %UMA% looked %YOU% up and down, and upon finding nothing suspicious, twitched an ear and politely waved goodbye.
    - Still trying to process what had just happened, %YOU% reflexively raised a hand in return.
    - A moment later, reality clicked into place.
    - (Wait... it's barely five in the morning. Did %SEX% really say a morning run? Seriously?)
    - Shock washed over %YOU%.
    - While plenty of diligent %UMA% at the academy kept up with morning runs, hitting the track this early was on an entirely different level of dedication.
    - 「Did this kid drink that %UMA% coffee too...? No, an %UMA% wouldn't feel the caffeine anywhere near as strongly as I do. That means she really woke up this early just to run!」
    - Looking back toward the path, %YOU% couldn't help but gaze after the fading figure of the Young %UMA%.
    - 「I forgot to ask for her name...」
    - Having crossed paths with the girl, %YOU% resumed idling around the predawn campus, hoping to run into %SEX% again.
    - Unfortunately, right up until the sun crested the horizon, %SEX% was nowhere to be seen.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Whatever... I'll head back to the office and take a nap. The debut selection races are today anyway.」
    - Indeed, today was the official Debut Selection Race organized by the academy, designed as a mutual draft between debuting %UMA% and trainers.
    - The girls would run with everything they had, and standout performers would receive contract offers from seasoned trainers.
    - %YOU% had originally planned to be well-rested and sharp for the event, but curiosity had gotten the better of %YOU% thanks to that damned specialty coffee.
    - Even though %YOU%'s body remained wired, mental exhaustion was setting in deep.
    - And so, %YOU% headed back to catch some shut-eye on the office couch.
    - But %YOU% had vastly underestimated the brew's lingering kick. Lying on the sofa and trying to clear all thoughts yielded nothing.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「I can't fall asleep at all. Might as well head down to the track early.」
    - Giving up on rest, %YOU% stood up and made tracks.
    - Arriving at the academy grounds, %YOU% found the turf course that would host today's selection trials.
    - In the early morning light, glistening dew drops still clung to the green blades of grass; the scene was serene and picturesque.
    - It still seemed a bit too early for anyone to be here... or was it?
    - %YOU% had assumed the field would be completely empty, but reality proved otherwise. Way down at the far end of the turf, a lone splash of orange moved across the track.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「It's %SEX%!」
    - To think that after parting ways on the road, the two would cross paths here once more. Seeing %SEX% again instantly banished %YOU%'s lingering lethargy.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Perfect chance. I can ask for her name this time.」
    - Seeing the Young %UMA% thoroughly absorbed in stride, %YOU% chose not to call out, leaning casually against the rail instead to observe from a professional trainer's vantage point.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Solid form, great drive... but isn't it a bit too unconstrained?」
    - %YOU% furrowed a brow, sensing that the Young %UMA%'s stride, while natural, lacked the structure of formal coaching.
    - Just as %YOU% was analyzing the mechanics, the girl rounded the bend and naturally spotted %YOU% standing near the rail.
    - Picking up the pace slightly, %SEX% coasted over toward %YOU% and eased into a stop.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Young %UMA%
        - 「Good morning, Trainer! I didn't expect to see you at the track!」
    - Wiping away a sheen of light sweat from her forehead with the back of her wrist, the girl offered a bright greeting.
    - %YOU% offered a warm nod in reply.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Young %UMA%
        - 「Trainer... did you not sleep well last night?」
    - Catching the bloodshot lines in %YOU%'s eyes, the girl asked with genuine concern.
    - 「It was all that coffee... Well, never mind that! Could you introduce yourself? Your running style caught my eye.」
    - Startled by the sudden barrage of interest, the girl blinked in momentary surprise.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Young %UMA%
        - 「My name is %CHARA%. The thing I love most is running. Um... that's about it.」
    - Giving the briefest of introductions, %CHARA% quietly trailed off into silence.
    - She clearly wasn't the chatty type.
    - Not knowing quite how to follow up, %YOU% felt a stiff smile freezing on your face.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Um, if there isn't anything else, I'll go back to running now.」
    - Lowering her gaze, %CHARA% politely made her way back onto the turf.
    - Watching %SEX% walk away, %YOU% shook your head with a wry smile. Wanting to learn more about her, the words had somehow failed to come out.
    - Taking a deep breath, %CHARA% fell back into a starting stance. %YOU% rested elbows on the rail, absently tapping fingers against the metal.
    - As %CHARA% surged down the track, %YOU% watched that retreating silhouette, and a bold thought suddenly struck like lightning.
    - (Does %SEX% already have a trainer...? If not, could I try recruiting %SEX%?)
    - The spark caught immediately, swelling in %YOU%'s mind until it crowded out everything else.
    - %YOU% resolved to ask her directly the next time she came around the bend.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Staff Member
        - 「Trainer, would you mind clearing the track for a bit? We need to prepare the grounds for the selection races.」
    - Just as %YOU% was ready to approach %CHARA%, event staff arrived to set up the course.
    - Caught flat-footed, %YOU% had no choice but to steal one last glance at the distant orange figure before stepping away.
    - ......
    - After killing time with endless laps around campus, the scheduled start of the selection races finally arrived.
    - %YOU% hurried to the track and managed to secure a prime spot right at the rail.
    - Then, gazing at the contenders warming up in the paddock, %YOU% froze in disbelief.
    - (You've got to be kidding me... %SEX% went for a dawn run on the morning of her own debut trial? That early?!)
    - Sure enough, %CHARA%, who %YOU% had already bumped into twice by sheer coincidence, stood among the jittery competitors, calmly going through her routine stretches.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Let's see what you're truly capable of...」
    - Soon, the official call came. The runners filed into their gates, took their marks, and braced for the bell.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Announcer
        - 「Clear skies and firm turf! The runners are loaded and ready—」
    - The gates snapped open!
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Announcer
        - 「A clean break across the board! Though they're yet to debut, the sheer potential in this field is palpable!」
    - The %UMA% surged forward like loosed arrows, galloping into full stride. In an instant, %YOU%'s eyes locked onto that brilliant blaze of orange.
    - 「A front-runner? Here I was wondering if you'd run pace or stalk from the midfield... That caught me off guard...」
    - %YOU% watched with rapt fascination as %CHARA% burst through the pack, seizing the outright lead.
    - But within seconds, %YOU% was stunned.
    - Having already captured the lead with ease, %CHARA% wasn't settling into a cruising pace—she was accelerating.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Announcer
        - 「Setting the pace is %CHARA%...! What incredible early burst, opening up daylight right out of the gate! But will she have enough left in the tank at this tempo?!」
    - Even the commentator sounded incredulous, mirroring the exact question hanging in %YOU%'s mind.
    - Sprinting straight from the bell—doesn't %SEX% fear hitting the wall in the final stretch?
    - Trainers around %YOU% began muttering among themselves, all eyes transfixed on %CHARA%'s suicidal pace.
    - Yet the girl at the center of it all simply dug deeper, finding another gear.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Announcer
        - 「%CHARA% is accelerating again! She's pulling away! A lead of five lengths over the field—and she's still pouring it on!」
    - Under the stunned gazes of the onlookers, %CHARA% widened the gap with every stride, slicing across the turf like a bolt of emerald lightning, until—
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Announcer
        - 「Two hundred meters... one hundred meters...! %CHARA% crosses the wire by a colossal margin! Wait, look at that clock... It's a new track record!」
    - The stands erupted into utter pandemonium.
    - Far from burning out or fading in the stretch, %CHARA% had maintained an unrelenting runaway sprint from wire to wire, putting on an absolute masterclass in dominance.
    - %YOU% couldn't hold back the surge of adrenaline for another second.
    - The moment the race concluded, %YOU% was among the first to vault over the rail and dash straight toward %CHARA%.
    - Behind %YOU%, dozens of trainers with the exact same idea were leaping over the fence in pursuit.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「%CHARA%! Please, let me—urk!」
    - In an unfortunate stroke of clumsiness, %YOU%'s own frantic feet got tangled, sending you tumbling into the grass. By the time you scrambled back up, a thick crowd of trainers had already swarmed %CHARA%.
    - %YOU% cursed under %YOU%'s breath, punching your own thigh in frustration.
    # FLAGNAME:15 = 当前声望
    - if: era.get('flag:15') < 1000
      acc: 1
      key: rec
      content: No, I can't give up like this. I still have a shot! (Pursue Recruitment) # Reputation: Rookie / Experienced
      lines:
        - Setting your jaw with determination, %YOU% shouldered into the clamoring crowd surrounding %CHARA%.
        - Pushing through the frenzy of eager trainers, %YOU% fought for every inch forward.
        - Suddenly, the surrounding crowd let out a chorus of groans and began to disperse in disappointment. %YOU% looked closer and saw that %CHARA% was already holding a signed contract.
        - The trainer who had secured her was someone %YOU% recognized—a respected senior trainer who had offered %YOU% guidance before, someone whose credentials far outshone %YOU%'s own.
        - (At least I don't have to worry about %CHARA%'s talent going to waste... Still, it stings so much.)
        - Swallowing the bitter pill of defeat, %YOU% quietly turned and walked away from the field.
    - if: era.get('flag:15') >= 1000
      acc: 2
      content: A top-tier trainer never lets a generational talent slip away. (Pursue Recruitment) # Reputation: Mid-rank / Elite / Legendary
      lines:
        - "Having witnessed %CHARA%'s breathtaking runaway showcase, %YOU% was utterly convinced: this girl was born to be a superstar."
        - All she needed was a trainer seasoned enough to guide that brilliance.
        - And %YOU% was precisely one of those respected %TITLE% trainers.
        - There was no way in the world %YOU% was going to hand %CHARA% over to anyone else.
        - Straightening your collar, %YOU% strode forward with commanding confidence, cutting straight toward the inner circle.
        - content:
            - fontWeight: bold
              content: Rookie Trainer A
            - 「Ah, it's %SIR% %YOURNAME%! Are you scouting for talent here too?」
        - content:
            - fontWeight: bold
              content: Rookie Trainer B
            - 「I had no idea %SIR% %YOURNAME% was keeping an eye on this trial!」
        - content:
            - fontWeight: bold
              content: Veteran Trainer C
            - 「If anyone has what it takes to polish a gem like %CHARA%, it's definitely %SIR% %YOURNAME%.」
        - ......
        - To %YOU%'s surprise, the surrounding trainers recognized %YOU% instantly, instinctively parting to create an open path.
        - Giving them polite nods of acknowledgement, %YOU% walked unhindered into the center of the gathering.
        - Thanks to their deference, %YOU% arrived just in time to see %CHARA% on the verge of signing with a senior trainer %YOU% knew well.
        - acc: 1
          content: 「Senior, %CHARA%, hold on just a moment, please.」
        - %YOU%'s firm voice drew their attention immediately.
        - content:
            - fontWeight: bold
              content: Senior Trainer
            - 「Trainer %YOURNAME%? Are you here to scout her as well?」
        - acc: 1
          content: 「I am. I believe %CHARA% possesses extraordinary potential, and I want to train her.」
        - The senior trainer frowned slightly, letting out a measured sigh.
        - Despite the deep respect %YOU% held for her, stepping aside when it came to a talent like %CHARA% was out of the question.
        - content:
            - fontWeight: bold
              content: Senior Trainer
            - 「I suppose that's fair. Exceptional %UMA% don't come around every day.」
        - It seemed she had no intention of backing down either.
        - color: %COLOR%
          content:
            - fontWeight: bold
              content: %CHARA%
            - 「Um... everyone...」
        - Sensing the palpable tension in the air, %CHARA% tried to ease the mood, but her timid voice barely made a dent.
        - "「How about this: since neither of us is willing to concede, we each take a day to coach %CHARA%, and let her performance decide who trains her. Fair?」"
        - %YOU% pitched the proposal right on the spot.
        - The senior trainer and %CHARA% both perked up, eyes widening.
        - content:
            - fontWeight: bold
              content: Senior Trainer
            - 「Not a bad idea. We can exchange coaching insights while we're at it. What do you think, Suzuka?」
        - color: %COLOR%
          content:
            - fontWeight: bold
              content: %CHARA%
            - 「I think that sounds wonderful! I'll be in both of your care!」
        - Seeing that both of them were on board, %YOU% breathed an inward sigh of relief.
        - acc: 1
          content: 「Then I'll leave %CHARA% in your capable hands tomorrow, Senior.」
        - content:
            - fontWeight: bold
              content: Senior Trainer
            - 「Agreed. I'll arrange the practice trial as well.」
        - The senior nodded briskly. %YOU% offered a polite wave and began walking toward the exit.
        - (I don't know what my odds are, but this is far better than sitting on my hands. I really want to train her...)
        - Casting one last look back at the senior trainer chatting with %CHARA%, %YOU% drew a steady breath and departed the track.
    - acc: 3
      content: With a crowd that thick, it's impossible. Time to catch up on sleep. (Abandon Recruitment)
      lines:
        - Gazing at the impenetrable sea of people surrounding her, %YOU% made the sensible choice to turn back.

after: # Rookie / Experienced, next visit to training ground
  title: After the Selection Race
  lines:
    - Sometime after the selection race, %YOU% found %YOU%'s footsteps wandering back toward the training grounds.
    - Although %YOU% knew %CHARA% would likely thrive under the senior trainer's tutelage, the bitter memory of losing out by a clumsy stumble still gnawed at %YOU%.
    - Today was supposed to be spent in the office, but an inexplicable urge drove %YOU% to see how the senior's team was progressing.
    - Grabbing a jacket, %YOU% headed straight to the track.
    - By now, several %UMA% were already running drills. It didn't take %YOU% long to spot %CHARA% among %THEY%.
    - %CHARA% was at the starting line going through warm-up stretches, with the senior trainer holding a stopwatch alongside the rest of the squad.
    - It seemed the senior was about to run a full mock race with her team.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Senior Trainer
        - 「On your marks... Get set... Go!」
    - With a sharp drop of the senior's arm, the runners broke together in unison.
    - Right on cue, %CHARA% surged into the lead with a burst of natural acceleration.
    - But just as %YOU% braced to watch another jaw-dropping runaway performance, %CHARA% deliberately dialed back her speed.
    - To %YOU%'s astonishment, %CHARA%'s expression shifted into visible discomfort as she throttled her pace, hovering barely half a length ahead of second place.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Is this some kind of new tactic? Did the senior devise a different race plan?」
    - Doubts swirling, %YOU% kept eyes glued to the track.
    - Multiple times, %CHARA% seemed poised to break away and open daylight, only to pull herself back every time.
    - Sensing an opening, the second-place %UMA% seized the moment and swept past %CHARA% along the flank.
    - %CHARA% fought furiously to reclaim the front, but the momentum was lost; another runner surged past her into second.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「This is bad... %SEX% looks completely rattled.」
    - Trapped in the middle of the pack, flanked on all sides by hard-charging opponents, %CHARA% scrambled frantically but couldn't break free.
    - Bit by bit, fatigue set in.
    - Despite %SEX% giving everything she had, opponent after opponent blew past her.
    - By the time the mock race concluded, %CHARA% crossed the line near the very back of the field.
    - Utterly exhausted, %SEX% didn't even have the energy to check her finishing time, collapsing against the outer rail, gasping for breath.
    - %YOU% frowned deeply. %CHARA% had the engine to blow fields away—how could a few days under a new regime leave her this gassed and demoralized?
    - %YOU% decided to speak with %CHARA% directly.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「%CHARA%, do you have a moment to talk?」
    - %CHARA%'s drooping ears immediately perked up.
    - %SEX% blinked, looking around until her eyes found %YOU%.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「It's the Trainer from before! Were you calling for me?」
    - %YOU% nodded, and %CHARA% walked over, her posture hesitant.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Did you need something from me, Trainer?」
    - acc: 1
      content: 「%CHARA%, did something feel off during that run just now?」
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Um, no... not really...」
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Are you feeling down or troubled?」
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「It's not that either...」
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Because from where I'm standing, Suzuka, it looked like you lost all belief in your stride.」
    - Flustered by %YOU%'s piercing observation, %CHARA% didn't even notice %YOU% shifting from formal address to her given name.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「I... I don't really know why it happens either...」
    - Her ears flattened back against her hair.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Lately... I think I might actually hate running.」
    - The confession hit %YOU% like a bucket of ice water. A race %UMA%, born to gallop, saying she hated to run?
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「My morning runs feel so pure and free, but the moment formal practice begins, all the energy drains right out of me. Everyone else pushes so hard, and I want to match their drive, but I just can't keep up...」
    - A lightbulb switched on in %YOU%'s mind.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Suzuka, are you saying you only hate running when you're in official training?」
    - %CHARA% froze, her eyes widening in surprise.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Y-Yes... that's right.」
    - acc: 1
      content: 「What goes through your mind during your early morning runs? How do they feel?」
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Well... when I run at dawn, the open road and the horizon ahead belong entirely to me. That feeling makes me happier than anything.」
    - acc: 1
      content: 「And what happens during team practice?」
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「At first I have that scenery all to myself, but then the others start closing in... and before I know it, I can't stop worrying about them.」
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Then why not run like you did in the selection trial—and leave them in the dust?」
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「My trainer says my stamina is meant for the finish line. %SEX% told me to stay close to the pack so I don't waste energy going out too fast.」
    - %YOU% paused in thought, piecing together the final puzzle.
    - 「I see. Your trainer wants you to conserve precious energy for a late kick, but %SEX% doesn't realize your stamina comes from having no one in front of you.」
    - As %YOU% laid out the truth with razor-sharp clarity, %CHARA% nodded, comprehension slowly dawning across her face.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Do you have any more mock runs scheduled for today?」
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Yes, quite a few.」
    - acc: 1
      content: 「On your next heat, try running like this...」
    - Leaning close to %CHARA%'s ear, %YOU% whispered a bold tactical adjustment. The girl's eyes lit with sudden fire.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Okay! I'll give it everything I have! Thank you, Trainer!」
    - Beaming with renewed energy, %CHARA% waved and bounded back toward her teammates.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Everything rides on this one run.」
    - %YOU% exhaled a long breath and waited intently.
    - Before long, the senior called her squad back to the barriers for their second mock trial.
    - %YOU% straightened up, eyes locked onto the field.
    - The runners dug their spikes into the turf, waiting for the signal.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Senior Trainer
        - 「On your marks... Get set... Go!」
    - The field exploded into motion once more—flawless breaks all around, just as expected of a top-tier stable.
    - %YOU% focused entirely on %CHARA%.
    - Sure enough, out of a textbook jump, %CHARA% instantly unleashed her explosive burst, seizing the rail.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「That's it, Suzuka! Go!」
    - This time, she didn't look back. %CHARA% poured on speed, opening up daylight stride by stride.
    - Even from a distance, %YOU% could see the radiant smile blooming across %CHARA%'s face.
    - It was the very same joy %SEX% had shown at the selection trial—a smile straight from the soul.
    - Soon came the final stretch, the critical juncture where her trainer had insisted she hold her ground.
    - %YOU%'s palms went clammy. If Suzuka couldn't hold this blistering margin to the wire, if she flamed out and collapsed, %YOU% would be formally accused of sabotaging a colleague's session.
    - With that senior's vast network across the association, %YOU%'s reputation would be destroyed, potentially ending %YOU%'s career on the spot.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Faster, Suzuka! Run away and don't look back!」
    - Clenching fists tight, %YOU% roared encouragement in %YOU%'s heart.
    - As if answering that silent plea, %CHARA% surged once more, storming across the finish line with an overwhelming advantage.
    - After crossing the wire, %CHARA% was full of vigor, showing no signs of the previous collapse.
    - A massive weight lifted off %YOU%'s shoulders.
    - Just as %YOU% raised a hand to wave %CHARA% over, %SEX% trotted straight to her senior trainer instead.
    - %YOU% watched as the two engaged in an intense discussion before both turning their eyes toward %YOU%.
    - Side by side, they walked directly over to where %YOU% stood.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Uh, good morning, Senior!」
    - %YOU% squeezed out a dry chuckle and an awkward greeting.
    - The senior and %CHARA% stared at %YOU% as if interrogating a prime suspect.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Senior Trainer
        - 「Suzuka defied my direct race orders just now. You put her up to this, didn't you?」
    - The senior gave %YOU%'s shoulder a solid shove. It wasn't painful, but %YOU% still averted %YOU%'s gaze sheepishly.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Senior Trainer
        - 「Suzuka just requested a transfer to your stable. It breaks my heart to let her go, but her performance today made her case undeniable. I've decided to hand her training over to you.」
    - %YOU% looked up, genuinely stunned.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Senior Trainer
        - 「I was too rigid, trapped by conventional wisdom. I only thought about pacing her stamina, completely blind to what drives her heart. Since you diagnosed what was truly wrong, you'd better shoulder that responsibility and raise Suzuka into a champion.」
    - She clapped a heavy hand on %YOU%'s shoulder.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Senior Trainer
        - 「I believe in your talent as a professional. Don't let me down, understood?」
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Count on it, Senior! I'll pour everything into Suzuka!」
    - The senior smiled warmly, before her tone turned sharp as a blade.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Senior Trainer
        - 「That said, meddling in another team's drills is a real offense. If I ever catch you squandering Suzuka's gift...」
    - Leaving that ominous warning hanging in the air, she spun on her heel and departed without another word.
    - %YOU% stood frozen under the weight of the threat, until a gentle tug on %YOU%'s sleeve broke the spell.
    - Turning around, %YOU% met %CHARA%'s wide, innocent eyes.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Um... will you sign a contract with me, Trainer?」
    - Watching the senior's silhouette fade into the distance, %YOU% let out a heartfelt sigh and finalized the paperwork with %CHARA%.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Suzuka, I only meant to give you some advice... I never dreamed I'd end up as your actual trainer.」
    - %CHARA% offered a tender smile.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - "「The moment you told me to run the way my heart truly desired, something shifted deep inside me. When I let go and ran free along that riverbank, I felt that pure, quiet joy from my morning runs wash over me again. Right then and there, I decided: wherever you lead, that's where I want to run.」"
    - Drawing in a deep, grateful breath, %YOU% smiled back.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「In that case, Miss %CHARA%, I look forward to working with you!」
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Yes! I'm looking forward to it as well!」
    - And so, through an unexpected twist of fate, %YOU% successfully welcomed %CHARA% into the fold.

tomorrow: # Mid-rank and above, next visit to training ground
  title: The Day After Selection
  lines:
    - Even though %YOU% barely slept the night before, today's schedule was firmly committed.
    - Tidying up quickly, %YOU% hurried down to the training grounds.
    - At this hour, several %UMA% were already engaged in drills. %YOU% picked out %CHARA% among them with ease.
    - %CHARA% was running through prep stretches at the gate, flanked by the senior holding a stopwatch alongside her teammates.
    - It seemed the senior had finished her briefing and was preparing a full-team mock trial.
    - Spotting %YOU%, the senior offered a brief nod before initiating the trial.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Senior Trainer
        - 「On your marks... Get set... Go!」
    - %YOU% watched as the senior's arm snapped downward, sending the field surging forward in lockstep.
    - Right out of the gate, %CHARA% accelerated cleanly to claim the lead.
    - %YOU% expected to see the senior's plan for blowing away the field, but %CHARA% abruptly reined in her own momentum.
    - To %YOU%'s astonishment, %CHARA% was maintaining a razor-thin lead of barely half a horse's length over second place.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Is this a new tactical approach? Does the senior have a grander scheme in mind?」
    - Plagued by doubts, %YOU% stayed focused on the race.
    - %YOU% clearly saw %CHARA% attempt to break away several times, only to second-guess herself and pull back every time.
    - Before long, the runner in second seized the opening, slicing past %CHARA% along the outer flank.
    - %CHARA% fought tooth and nail to reclaim the front, but could never find the opening, falling behind third place as well.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「This is bad... %SEX% looks completely rattled.」
    - Hemmed in by the pack, boxed from front to back, left to right, %CHARA% twisted and pushed but couldn't break the siege.
    - Gradually, exhaustion crept into her stride.
    - Despite %SEX% giving every ounce of grit, runner after runner surged past.
    - In the end, %CHARA% finished near the very bottom of the order.
    - %SEX% didn't even have the strength left to check the timer, leaning against the rail in ragged, gasping breaths.
    - Rather than disturbing the utterly exhausted %CHARA%, %YOU% offered a quiet wave to the senior and stepped away from the track.
    - The outcome of this trial ran completely counter to %YOU%'s expectations.
    - By all rights, a front-runner like %CHARA% possessed ample stamina reserves; a single middle-distance workout should never have left %SEX% this completely spent.
    - What's more, speed was her undisputed greatest asset—how could she be overtaken so effortlessly from behind?
    - %YOU% had already drafted a comprehensive curriculum for %CHARA%, but it now seemed utterly ill-suited to her situation.
    - (This girl isn't a conventional front-runner... Tailoring a strategy that truly fits her will take dedicated, patient observation...)
    - %YOU% chalked up %CHARA%'s dismal trial to mismatched tactical coaching; after all, her sheer dominance at the debut selection trial was undeniable.
    - Ruffling %YOU%'s hair in mild frustration, %YOU% sighed.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Nothing else to do for now. We'll take it one step at a time.」

tomorrow_after_tomorrow: # After [The Day After Selection], same week, training ground
  title: Two Days After Selection
  lines:
    - Today was the day %YOU% was slated to coach %CHARA%, so %YOU% arose long before sunrise.
    - After a quick wash, %YOU% arrived at the track just as the first pale light was breaking over the horizon.
    - Fighting off a yawn, %YOU% caught a familiar orange silhouette out of the corner of %YOU%'s eye.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Haah... haah... Good morning, Trainer!」
    - Just like their very first encounter, %CHARA% was out on a solo dawn run. Spotting %YOU%, %SEX% jogged over with a bright greeting.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Good morning, Miss Suzuka. I thought I was early, but you're already in the middle of your workout.」
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Yes! I'm used to getting up early to run every day, so I don't feel sleepy at all.」
    - Looking at the pure, heartfelt smile on %CHARA%'s face, %YOU% felt a gentle stir inside.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「So, Trainer, what's the plan for today?」
    - Seeing %YOU% pause in thought, %CHARA% tilted her head in innocent curiosity.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Well, about today's training...」
    - %YOU% felt a pang of embarrassment; a single day was hardly enough time to draft a bespoke regimen from scratch.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Ah, right! Miss Suzuka, how did yesterday's training feel to you?」
    - %YOU% decided to gather more firsthand information on %CHARA%'s condition.
    - Surprisingly, %CHARA% lowered her head with a look of quiet dejection.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Honestly... I didn't really like it... Even though the track was the same, everyone was watching me, and bit by bit my strength just faded away...」
    - Hearing that confession, %YOU% fell into deep contemplation.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Then, Miss Suzuka, what do you feel when you run at dawn?」
    - The instant the question was asked, the girl's eyes lit up like stars.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「During my morning runs, I can fully take in the view out in front and along the sides. Before I know it, I've run so far, and I never feel tired at all when I finish.」
    - That seemed to pinpoint the exact heart of the matter.
    - acc: 1
      content: "「One last question: what guidance did the senior give you?」"
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「She felt my stamina was better suited for later, so she asked me not to pull too far ahead of the others so I wouldn't waste energy running too fast.」
    - %CHARA% seemed a little puzzled, but answered %YOU%'s question with total honesty.
    - By now, %YOU% had pieced together the outline of a real solution.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Miss Suzuka, we'll set formal drills aside for now. Right now, there's somewhere I want to take you.」
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Eh??」

river: # After [Two Days After Selection], same week, Outing - Riverbank
  title: The Riverbank
  lines:
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Um, Trainer?」
    - %YOU% led %CHARA% away from the training grounds and down toward the open riverbank. Along the way, %CHARA% tried asking about %YOU%'s intentions several times, but %YOU% kept things teasingly vague.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Here we are, Suzuka.」
    - %CHARA% glanced around, clearly struggling to decipher what %YOU% had in mind.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「I recall you mentioning that what you love most is having an open horizon all to yourself, right?」
    - %CHARA% gave a slightly bashful nod, looking out across the landscape as understanding began to bloom.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Then go ahead. Run along this riverbank to your heart's content.」
    - Unable to conceal the thrill bubbling up inside, %CHARA% dropped into a starting stance before %YOU% could even give the order.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Ready... Go!」
    - %YOU% watched as %CHARA% rocketed forward like a shooting star, breathing a quiet sigh of relief.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「I knew it. %SEX% has world-class talent—she just needed the right direction.」
    - Clearly, the senior had treated %CHARA%, a girl blessed with transcendent runaway pacing, as an ordinary front-runner who merely needed to manage her stamina.
    - Nodding to yourself, %YOU% waited quietly by the bank.
    - Before long, %CHARA% looped back around to where %YOU% stood. Seeing the genuine, radiant smile on her face, %YOU%'s heart was completely at ease.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「How did that feel, Suzuka?」
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「It felt incredible, Trainer! Right now... right now I feel full of energy, like I could easily run another lap!」
    - %YOU% smiled and held up a hand.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「No rush. You'll have plenty of chances to run. Come on, let's head back to the academy.」
    - %CHARA% gave an obedient, happy nod.

beginning: # After [The Riverbank], same week, next visit to training ground
  title: A Fresh Start
  lines:
    - When %YOU% and %CHARA% returned to the Tracen Academy training grounds, you crossed paths with the senior trainer bringing her squad out for practice.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Senior Trainer
        - 「Well now, Trainer %YOURNAME%, Suzuka. What a coincidence bumping into you two right as we arrived.」
    - %YOU% and %CHARA% exchanged a knowing smile.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Senior, when would it be convenient to hold the practice trial?」
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Senior Trainer
        - 「A trial already? Trainer %YOURNAME%, didn't you just take over Suzuka's coaching today?」
    - acc: 1
      content: 「I've had a thorough talk with Suzuka. Rather than relying on rushed drill plans, I place my faith in her innate strength.」
    - The senior stared at %YOU% in astonishment for a good while, only looking away once she saw that %YOU% wasn't joking in the slightest.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Senior Trainer
        - 「Fair enough. I'll set up a mock race right now. Let's see if your instincts hold up.」
    - The senior quickly gathered her team together to prepare the workout.
    - %YOU% watched as %CHARA% joined the line and stepped onto the turf.
    - The senior's runners lined up at the starting mark, poised for the break.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Senior Trainer
        - 「On your marks... Get set... Go!」
    - The field surged forward in unison—an impeccable break, thoroughly worthy of the senior's top-notch stable.
    - In the next breath, %YOU% locked all attention onto %CHARA%.
    - Sure enough, off a crisp launch, %CHARA% uncorked her signature burst, claiming the pole position in the blink of an eye.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「That's it, Suzuka!」
    - Continuing to pour on speed, %CHARA% widened her cushion over second place stride by stride.
    - Even though the runners were already far down the backstretch, %YOU% could practically picture the smile lighting up %CHARA%'s face.
    - It was that true, uninhibited joy %SEX% had shown at the selection trial and on the riverbank.
    - Soon came the home turn—the ultimate test of an %UMA%'s stamina and sheer will.
    - A cold chill ran down %YOU%'s spine. Despite %YOU%'s unwavering faith in %CHARA%, %SEX% was still light on formal race experience; if her reserves gave out and she faltered in the stretch...
    - Her finishing time might turn out even worse than yesterday's trial.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Faster, Suzuka! Run away boldly!」
    - %YOU% clenched fists tight, cheering %CHARA% on with every fiber of %YOU%'s being.
    - As though hearing that silent roar, %CHARA% surged once more, storming home with an overwhelming lead to claim the wire.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Yes!」
    - %YOU% let out a triumphant cheer under %YOU%'s breath.
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Trainer, did you see? I never gave up the view in front for a single second!」
    - Crossing the line, %CHARA% didn't slow to a halt, trotting straight to %YOU%'s side with light, rhythmic pants.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Magnificent run, Suzuka. It seems my judgment was right on the mark.」
    - %YOU% offered %CHARA% an emphatic thumbs-up.
    - content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: Senior Trainer
        - 「Since the verdict is clear, I won't hold you up any longer. That said, while I respect your professional eye as a trainer, make sure you treasure Suzuka's gift.」
    - Walking over, the senior's voice held an unmistakable trace of envy. Still, after delivering that parting reminder, she turned and made her exit.
    - %YOU% waved goodbye to the senior, exchanging another smile with %CHARA% at %YOU%'s side.
    - acc: 1
      content: 「Well then, Miss %CHARA%, I look forward to working with you!」
    - color: %COLOR%
      content:
        - fontWeight: bold
          content: %CHARA%
        - 「Yes! I look forward to working with you too!」
    - In the end, %YOU% demonstrated your true coaching credentials, successfully bringing %CHARA% onto the team.
